<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Carpetani</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 179 BCE (approx.) · capital Toletum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A people of the central Meseta around Toledo and Madrid, defeated by Hannibal on the Tagus before Rome absorbed their lands.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Carpetani occupied the upper and middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a> basin, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciudad-real">Ciudad Real</a>, from the second half of the first millennium BCE. Their language is thought to have been Celtic, though Iberian influences were strong.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in fortified towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toletum</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/complutum">Complutum</a>, on a farming and herding economy of the open plateau. Their political organisation is little known, but they could field large armies. In 220 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> defeated a coalition of Carpetani, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/olcades">Olcades</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vaccaei">Vaccaei</a> at the crossing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> reached their land in the early 2nd century BCE: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-fulvius-nobilior">Marcus Fulvius Nobilior</a> won a battle near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toletum</a> in 193 BCE and took the town in 192 BCE, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius-sempronius-gracchus-consul-177-bc">Tiberius Sempronius Gracchus</a> pacified the region by 179 BCE. They became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>, and Toletum grew into Roman and later Visigothic Toledo.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 500 BCE – 179 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:49.75%;width:6.39%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 179 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Toletum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Carpetanians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-340&amp;focus=carpetani" aria-label="Carpetani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4581 751 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Carpetani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4901 1007L4975 1081M4901 1007L5031 967"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4975 1081h0M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4901 1007h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4901 1007h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Toletum. <a href="/atlas?year=-340&amp;focus=carpetani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
